data.content:
Created two files:

**`SortableList.razor`** — Renders a `<ul>` with each item using `@ItemTemplate`, plus "Move Up" / "Move Down" buttons. Uses `@key` for efficient diffing and disables buttons at boundaries.

**`SortableList.razor.cs`** — `partial class SortableList<TItem>`:
- **Copies** `Items` into a private `_items` list in `OnParametersSet` (never mutates the parent's list).
- Swap logic in `MoveUp`/`MoveDown` notifies the parent via `EventCallback<IReadOnlyList<TItem>>`.

Usage matches your example — just note the callback receives `IReadOnlyList<TItem>`:

```razor
<SortableList Items="@tasks" OnOrderChanged="HandleReorder">
    <ItemTemplate>
        <span>@context.Title</span>
    </ItemTemplate>
</SortableList>

@code {
    private List<TaskItem> tasks = [ /* ... */ ];

    private void HandleReorder(IReadOnlyList<TaskItem> updated)
    {
        tasks = updated.ToList();
    }
}
```
